le:","position":{"start":{"line":90,"column":1,"offset":3052},"end":{"line":90,"column":148,"offset":3199}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":90,"column":1,"offset":3052},"end":{"line":90,"column":148,"offset":3199}}},{"type":"code","lang":"text","meta":null,"value":"src/example/example.s\r\nsrc/example/example.ld","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1,"offset":3203},"end":{"line":95,"column":4,"offset":3262}},"data":{"highlightId":"code-4"}},{"type":"mdxJsxFlowElement","name":"ArticleSection","attributes":[{"type":"mdxJsxAttribute","name":"name","value":"Development Environment","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":17,"offset":3282},"end":{"line":97,"column":47,"offset":3312}}},{"type":"mdxJsxAttribute","name":"id","value":"development-environment","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":48,"offset":3313},"end":{"line":97,"column":76,"offset":3341}}},{"type":"mdxJsxAttribute","name":"level","value":"h2","position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":77,"offset":3342},"end":{"line":97,"column":87,"offset":3352}}}],"children":[],"position":{"start":{"line":97,"column":1,"offset":3266},"end":{"line":97,"column":90,"offset":3355}}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the best development experience, consider installing the ","position":{"start":{"line":99,"column":1,"offset":3359},"end":{"line":99,"column":62,"offset":3420}}},{"type":"link","title":null,"url":"https://github.com/deanmlittle/vscode-sbpf-asm","children":[{"type":"text","value":"VS Code sBPF Assembly extension","position":{"start":{"line":99,"column":63,"offset":3421},"end":{"line":99,"column":94,"offset":3452}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":99,"column":62,"offset":3420},"end":{"line":99,"column":143,"offset":3501}}},{"type":"text","value":" which provides:","position":{"start":{"line":99,"column":143,"offset":3501},"end":{"line":99,"column":159,"offset":3517}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":99,"column":1,"offset":3359},"end":{"line":99,"column":159,"offset":3517}}},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"spread":false,"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":false,"checked":null,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Syntax highlighting for sBPF assembly","position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":3,"offset":3521},"end":{"line":100,"column":40,"offset":3558}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":3,"offset":3521},"end":{"line":100,"column":40,"offset":3558}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1,"offset":3519},"end":{"line":100,"column":40,"offset":3558}}},{"type":"listItem","spread":false,"checked":null,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code completion for instructions and registers","position":{"start":{"line":101,"column":3,"offset":3562},"end":{"line":101,"column":49,"offset":3608}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":101,"column":3,"offset":3562},"end":{"line":101,"column":49,"offset":3608}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":101,"column":1,"offset":3560},"end":{"line":101,"column":49,"offset":3608}}},{"type":"listItem","spread":false,"checked":null,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error detection and warnings","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":3,"offset":3612},"end":{"line":102,"column":31,"offset":3640}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":3,"offset":3612},"end":{"line":102,"column":31,"offset":3640}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1,"offset":3610},"end":{"line":102,"column":31,"offset":3640}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1,"offset":3519},"end":{"line":102,"column":31,"offset":3640}}}],"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1,"offset":0},"end":{"line":103,"column":1,"offset":3642}}},"raw":"import { ArticleSection } from \"../../../../components/ArticleSection/ArticleSection\";\r\n\r\n# Tooling\r\n\r\nWriting and building sBPF Assembly programs traditionally required the full Solana toolchain, which can be complex to set up and platform-dependent. For this exact reason, [Dean](https://x.com/deanmlittle), with contribution from [Claire](https://x.com/clairefxyz), created sBPF: a complete toolkit for creating and building sBPF Assembly programs.\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Installation\" id=\"installation\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nWe start by installing the package by doing:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncargo install --git https://github.com/Kiloshift-gg/sbpf.git\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter that we'll be able to do all the following commands:\r\n- `init`: Create a new project scaffold.\r\n- `build`: Compile into a Solana program executable.\r\n- `deploy`: Build and deploy the program.\r\n- `test`: Test the deployed program.\r\n- `e2e`: Build, deploy, and test a program.\r\n- `clean`: Clean up build and deploy artifacts.\r\n- `help`: Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s).\r\n\r\n```text\r\nUsage: sbpf <COMMAND>\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  init    Create a new project scaffold\r\n  build   Compile into a Solana program executable\r\n  deploy  Build and deploy the program\r\n  test    Test deployed program\r\n  e2e     Build, deploy and test a program\r\n  clean   Clean up build and deploy artifacts\r\n  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -h, --help     Print help\r\n  -V, --version  Print version\r\n```\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Initialize a new project\" id=\"initialize-a-new-project\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nTo create a new project, use the `sbpf init` command. By default, it initializes a project with Rust tests using Mollusk. You can also initialize a project with TypeScript tests using the `--ts-tests` option.\r\n\r\n```text\r\nsbpf init --help\r\nCreate a new project scaffold\r\n\r\nUsage: sbpf init [OPTIONS] [NAME]\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\n  [NAME]  The name of the project to create\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -t, --ts-tests  Initialize with TypeScript tests instead of Mollusk Rust tests\r\n  -h, --help      Print help information\r\n  -V, --version   Print version information\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter initializing the project, you can navigate into the project directory and use other commands to build, deploy, and test your program.\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Building Programs\" id=\"building-programs\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nsBPF provides two build options depending on your setup and needs:\r\n\r\n### sBPF Build\r\n\r\nThe build command uses a standalone assembler that requires no additional dependencies. It's perfect for learning and experimentation since it \"just works\" on any platform.\r\n\r\n```\r\nsbpf build\r\n```\r\n\r\n{/*\r\n\r\nTODO: Update sbpf to enable llvm build as an optional configuration then reenable this\r\n\r\n### Full Build\r\n\r\nThe standard build command provides integration with the complete Solana toolchain and project management features. \r\n\r\n> This requires the [Solana Command Line Tools](https://docs.anza.xyz/cli/install/) to be installed.\r\n\r\n```\r\nsbpf build\r\n``` */}\r\n\r\n### Advanced Usage\r\n\r\nYou can override the default linker with a custom linker file by including it in the src directory with the same name as your program. For example:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nsrc/example/example.s\r\nsrc/example/example.ld\r\n```\r\n\r\n<ArticleSection name=\"Development Environment\" id=\"development-environment\" level=\"h2\" />\r\n\r\nFor the best development experience, consider installing the [VS Code sBPF Assembly extension](https://github.com/deanmlittle/vscode-sbpf-asm) which provides:\r\n- Syntax highlighting for sBPF assembly\r\n- Code completion for instructions and registers\r\n- Error detection and warnings\r\n","highlightedCode":{"code-0":{"lang":"text","hast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"pre","properties":{"class":"shiki Kiloshift","style":"background-color:#11141a;color:#f6f6f4","tabindex":"0"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"cargo install --git https://github.com/Kiloshift-gg/sbpf.git"}]}]}]}]}]}},"code-1":{"lang":"text","hast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"pre","properties":{"class":"shiki Kiloshift","style":"background-color:#11141a;color:#f6f6f4","tabindex":"0"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage: sbpf <COMMAND>"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":""}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commands:"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"  init    Create a new project scaffold"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"  build   Compile into a Solana program executable"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"  deploy  Build and deploy the program"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"class":"line"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"  test    Test deployed program"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"cl